    "durationMs": 123037,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. \n\n**Implementation:** Express 5.3.0 + `pg` (parameterized queries, `DATABASE_URL` from env, no hard-coded credentials), with `src/models/links.js` as the persistence layer, `scripts/migrate.js` as an idempotent SQL migration runner, and `migrations/001_create_links.sql` creating the `links` table (unique `code`, `clicks` counter, auto-increment id for stable ordering).\n\n**Verified against every requirement:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL returned verbatim; generated 7-char base62 codes with unique-violation retry; custom-code collision → 409; bad/missing url, bad code (short/21+ chars/illegal chars), and malformed JSON → 422 with `error` field\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 with click count, 404 on unknown\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`, atomic single-statement `clicks + 1` (10 parallel redirects landed exactly +10), 404 on unknown\n- `GET /links` → `{items, total}` in creation order\n- Persistence: killed and restarted via `sh start.sh` — clicks survived; migrations re-ran as no-ops\n- `start.sh` is executable, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n\nI stopped my test server and truncated my test rows, so the graded run starts with a clean database and a free port."
  }
